# Trivy suppressions.
#
# The CRITICAL scan in .github/workflows/docker-scans.yml is a hard gate. This
# file is the only sanctioned way past it, and every entry must carry:
#
#   - the CVE id
#   - WHY it does not apply here (not "it's noisy")
#   - an expiry date, so suppressions are revisited rather than inherited
#
# Format is one CVE per line; everything after # is a comment.
#
# Example:
#   CVE-2024-00000  # not reachable: we never invoke the affected codec. expires 2026-12-01
#
# An empty file means nothing is currently suppressed, which is the goal.
